    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'll look into canary deployments. One thing though—in my experience, even with all those gates, it feels like there are these weird, unpredictable 'glitches' that just seem to pop up out of nowhere and mess everything up. Like, you do everything right, but something small and malicious still manages to sneak past the guards and break the system. Is there a way to specifically protect against those kinds of unpredictable, rogue elements that bypass the standard checks?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
